#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cono-check — Cono's checking component as a local web app: a live
digital twin of the page on your desk.

The camera watches your page; the page diffs the video locally, and only
when you pause writing does one frame go to Claude (`claude` CLI — your
Claude Code login, no API key), which streams back, fast fields first:

  visibility n/10   what the camera can actually see
  problem card      the question you're on, your progress, a Next button
  check             hint-first: where the mistake is, never the answer
  readability map   green/red page-shaped grid: what could/couldn't be read
  equations         the relations the problem runs on, ? for unknowns
  on your page      faithful transcription, student's errors preserved

The twin is the product: problem card + dialogue (typed chat, point with
your pen by clicking the image), equations, readability map. Replies
stream — first text in ~1-3 s.

Usage:
  cono-check                     # the Desk View camera (top-down on your desk) - the default
  cono-check browser             # fallback: any browser camera (iPhone Continuity, webcam)
  cono-check session             # 10-minute recorded session (Desk View)
  cono-check demo                # no camera needed: bundled sample session (demo chem = chemistry)
  cono-check doctor              # preflight: is everything ready to run?
  cono-check --model opus        # pick the model (default: sonnet)
  cono-check --replay DIR        # replay any recorded session directory
  cono-check --port 9000         # serve somewhere else (default: 8764)
  cono-check --no-contrast       # don't contrast-normalize snaps before reading
  cono-check --no-open           # don't open the browser automatically
Ctrl-C to stop.

Snaps get automatic contrast normalization (histogram stretch) before the
model reads them - a near-no-op on well-lit pages, a real lift on faint
pencil. Browser snaps are stretched on the canvas before upload; deskview/
replay frames are stretched in place server-side when Pillow is installed
(optional - everything works without it). The stored snap, the thumbnail,
and what the model reads are always the same pixels. Toggle live with the
"auto contrast" button under the camera, or start with --no-contrast.

Test feature: a "check stages" strip in the side column traces each
in-flight check/chat through the real pipeline stages (contrast, sent,
first streamed word, then each reply section as it arrives) with elapsed
time - driven by server events, never a timer. Toggle it with the
"stage trace" button; per-stage ms is logged into session bundles and
tabled by tools/score-session.py.
"""
